    "peakVelocityPressure": "DIN EN 1991-1-4/NA Table NA.B.2: qp(z) = 1.5 qb (z ≤ 7 m), 1.7 qb (z/10)^0.37 (7-50 m), 2.1 qb (z/10)^0.24 (50-300 m) inland; 1.8 qb (z ≤ 4 m), 2.3 qb (z/10)^0.27, 2.6 qb (z/10)^0.19 at the coast; 1.1 kN/m² (z ≤ 2 m), 1.5 (z/10)^0.19 kN/m² on the North Sea islands; qb = ½ ρ vb² (ρ 1.25 kg/m³). Table NA.B.3 (simplified, buildings up to 25 m: the whole height at the step of h) is used where the project sets wind.peakVelocityPressure.useSimplified (Code Values); the EN terrain categories 0-IV stay available with EN Eq 4.8",
